# Enter in the composer REPLIES to the open thread; it does not start a new one.
#
# The Enter listener is attached once and lives for the field's whole life, so
# it cannot capture the kickoff/reply decision — it used to, froze it as
# "kickoff" on a pre-load frame, and every Enter thereafter created a session
# while the Send button (recomputed per frame) replied correctly.
#
# settings: {"window_width":1100,"window_height":760,"open_tabs":["t2"],"active_tab":"t2","theme":"dark"}

require_thread t2

expect_text "needs a decision"

# Focus the composer BY NAME. This was `click 646 674` — a literal point four
# pixels inside the field's top edge — and feat/vis-statusmove moved the whole
# composer 26px down (hanabi reserved a status strip at the window's floor that
# Puffin has no equivalent of; layout_system.h). The point then landed on the
# transcript, the typing went nowhere, and six scripts in this directory failed
# on one edit. `click_ui` takes the widget's centre, so it cannot break on
# layout again.
click_ui composer_reply_input
wait_frames 4
type "enter should reply here"
wait_frames 4
key ENTER
wait_frames 40

# Still the same thread: its title, and its existing content, are both present.
expect_text "needs a decision"
expect_text "Reconciled 4,812 accounts"
expect_text "enter should reply here"
